  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Сейчас префект перережет нашу ленту.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Right now the prefect will cut our ribbon.' Mikhail anchors the line on 'now', while 'ribbon' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Аплодисменты, дамы и господа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Applause, ladies and gentlemen!' The grammar packs 'applause' and 'gentlemen' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Добро пожаловать в отель!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Welcome to the hotel!' Mikhail anchors the line on 'good', while 'hotel' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "А где моя пицца?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And where is my pizza?' Mikhail pairs 'where' with 'pizza' directly, since spoken Russian skips English filler words like 'the', 'a', and 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Всё будет. Не беспокойся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everything will be ready. Do not worry.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'everything' before landing on 'worry'. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Приехала горячая пицца, доставка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The hot pizza arrived, delivery.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'came' before landing on 'delivery'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Кто здесь шеф Баринов?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who here is Chef Barinov?' The meaning hinges on 'who' working together with 'proper name' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Давайте сюда, проверяйте заказ.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hand it here, check the order.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'let's' and 'here' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "У меня всё готово.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I have everything ready.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'at' and 'me' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Где наши красивые лепестки?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where are our beautiful rose petals?' In Russian, the idea of 'where' flows naturally into 'rose petals' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Они на складе в коробке.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They are in the storage room in a box.' The meaning hinges on 'they' working together with 'in the box' in spoken Russian. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я сейчас принесу эту коробку.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
